codex
The prior digest-phase regression is green (exit 0), but the new collection-phase adversarial test is genuinely red (exit 1): when an entry was listed/Lstat’d as a directory and the root path is replaced by a file before the root recheck, the scoped walk reclassifies it as a file leaf and can omit descendants. That diverges from `fs.WalkDir`, which still attempts descent based on the listed `DirEntry` and fails closed. I’m stopping release/performance gates here because this trust-boundary failure makes them non-creditable; I’ll persist the exact test and evidence for developer rework.
